# FMT-B regression fixture (Round XXXVI — graduated from
# `tests/fixtures/known_gaps/fmt_multiline_arg_indent.gg`).
#
# Reduction of the `driver.gg:833-838` shape from the aborted D27
# Round A fmt sweep: a call arg containing a multi-line binary chain
# used to be rendered with the chain's continuation lines at column 4
# (from a fresh sub-Emitter starting at indent=0), instead of matching
# the outer call's indent. The reformatted output still parsed on this
# minimal repro but the visual indent was wrong; on the wider driver.gg
# context the reflow cascaded into an SH-driver
# E_MoveInOperandPosition (43 phantom diagnostics) that broke bootstrap.
#
# Round XXXVI FMT-B: `element_to_string` now seeds the sub-Emitter's
# indent from the caller's context so internal newlines from the
# sub-render land at the correct column.
#
# R41 T-FMT-D: the message was LENGTHENED when `MAX_WIDTH` rose to 120. At the
# old width the chain broke; at 120 the original text fit on one line and the
# paired test's assertion loop stopped executing entirely — a pin that is green
# because it never runs is worse than no pin (Core #12). The chain must stay
# wider than the budget for the continuation-column assertion to mean anything.
from std.io import stderr

void main():
    String backend = "llvm"
    print(("error: unsupported --backend=" + backend + " (the self-host compiler emits C only; use --backend=c, or rebuild with the LLVM backend enabled)"), file=stderr)
